From: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: add force suspend/resume to system sleep callbacks

When a port is open at system suspend, the runtime-PM usage count of the
serial engine stays elevated and its runtime-suspend callback never runs,
so the GENI clocks and interconnect votes stay up for the whole sleep.
On the AYN Odin 3 the Bluetooth HCI and gamepad MCU serdev ports are
always open, which keeps the QUP wrapper clocked, holds a CNOC vote in
the RPMh sleep set, and stops the SoC from ever reaching CX shutdown in
suspend-to-idle: about 240 mA during a 10 minute nap versus 5 mA with
both ports closed.

Call pm_runtime_force_suspend() at the end of the system-suspend callback
so the runtime-suspend path always gates the resources, skipping only a
console whose suspend is disabled, and pm_runtime_force_resume() at the
start of the resume callback to restore them before the port is resumed.

Backport of the mainline change to Linux 7.2 on top of Armada's 1006
(the non-console IRQ mask in the same two functions).

Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit d0cd9c8d0fd59bc7d140f3d60cf02e1d80376dab)

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1975,6 +1975,7 @@
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
+	int ret;
 
 	/*
 	 * A peer that keeps streaming into a non-console geni UART across the
@@ -2001,7 +2002,19 @@
 		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
 		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	}
-	return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+
+	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * When no_console_suspend is set the console must remain active
+	 * across system sleep, so skip the force suspend path.
+	 */
+	if (!console_suspend_enabled && uart_console(uport))
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -2011,6 +2024,10 @@
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
+	ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 	/* Balance the disable_irq() taken in qcom_geni_serial_suspend(). */
 	if (!uart_console(uport))
